 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Sandboxed Tool Agent\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates the **sandboxed tool agent** pattern — Claude operating inside a strict tool boundary where:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Only explicitly permitted tools are exposed (no dynamic tool registration)\n",
    "- Each tool carries its own credential scope — no credential is shared across tools\n",
    "- Claude streams its reasoning and tool calls in real time\n",
    "- The sandbox enforces blast radius control: compromise of one tool's credentials doesn't expose others\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why this pattern matters\n",
    "\n",
    "Most agentic systems give Claude broad tool access. For high-stakes domains (infrastructure, billing, access control), this creates unnecessary risk. The sandboxed tool agent inverts the default:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Allowlist, not blocklist** — Claude can only call tools explicitly registered in the sandbox\n",
    "- **Per-tool credential isolation** — each tool uses the minimum credential needed for its job\n",
    "- **No write access by default** — read-only tools answer 95% of support questions\n",
    "\n",
    "## Use case: Infrastructure support agent\n",
    "\n",
    "A support engineer asks: *\"Why can't account 123456789012 run EC2 instances?\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "Claude has three tools:\n",
    "1. `lookup_account` — current account state (read-only DB)\n",
    "2. `lookup_policy` — active policy evaluation (read-only org API)\n",
    "3. `get_audit_trail` — recent activity (scoped read-only credentials per account)\n",
    "\n",
    "Claude decides which tools to call, in what order, and synthesises the answer — without any write access to any system.\n",
    "\n",
    "## DEMO_MODE\n",
    "\n",
    "Set `DEMO_MODE = True` (default) to run with mock tool responses — no API credentials needed beyond `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`.\n",
    "Set `DEMO_MODE = False` to wire in real tool implementations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%pip install anthropic --quiet"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "import os\n",
    "from typing import Any\n",
    "\n",
    "import anthropic\n",
    "\n",
    "DEMO_MODE = True  # Set False to use real tool implementations\n",
    "MODEL = \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n",
    "\n",
    "client = anthropic.Anthropic(api_key=os.environ.get(\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\", \"your-api-key\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Tool Definitions\n",
    "\n",
    "The sandbox exposes exactly three tools. These definitions are built server-side and never influenced by the client.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each tool's description is precise — Claude uses it to decide *when* to call the tool and *what arguments* to pass."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "TOOL_DEFINITIONS = [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"name\": \"lookup_account\",\n",
    "        \"description\": (\n",
    "            \"Look up current account state and recent assignment history. \"\n",
    "            \"Returns status, assigned lab, start/expiry times, and last 5 assignments. \"\n",
    "            \"Use this first to understand the account's current situation.\"\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "        \"input_schema\": {\n",
    "            \"type\": \"object\",\n",
    "            \"properties\": {\n",
    "                \"account_id\": {\n",
    "                    \"type\": \"string\",\n",
    "                    \"description\": \"12-digit cloud account ID\"\n",
    "                }\n",
    "            },\n",
    "            \"required\": [\"account_id\"]\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"name\": \"lookup_policy\",\n",
    "        \"description\": (\n",
    "            \"Look up the active policies applied to an account and evaluate whether \"\n",
    "            \"a specific action is denied. Returns plain-English summary of deny rules. \"\n",
    "            \"Use when the account exists but something is blocked.\"\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "        \"input_schema\": {\n",
    "            \"type\": \"object\",\n",
    "            \"properties\": {\n",
    "                \"account_id\": {\n",
    "                    \"type\": \"string\",\n",
    "                    \"description\": \"12-digit cloud account ID\"\n",
    "                },\n",
    "                \"action\": {\n",
    "                    \"type\": \"string\",\n",
    "                    \"description\": \"Optional. Specific action to check (e.g. 'ec2:RunInstances'). If omitted, returns all active deny rules.\"\n",
    "                }\n",
    "            },\n",
    "            \"required\": [\"account_id\"]\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"name\": \"get_audit_trail\",\n",
    "        \"description\": (\n",
    "            \"Fetch recent activity inside an account — who did what, when, from where. \"\n",
    "            \"Uses short-lived credentials scoped to this account only. \"\n",
    "            \"Use to investigate recent changes or suspicious activity.\"\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "        \"input_schema\": {\n",
    "            \"type\": \"object\",\n",
    "            \"properties\": {\n",
    "                \"account_id\": {\n",
    "                    \"type\": \"string\",\n",
    "                    \"description\": \"12-digit cloud account ID\"\n",
    "                },\n",
    "                \"hours\": {\n",
    "                    \"type\": \"integer\",\n",
    "                    \"description\": \"How many hours of history to fetch (default: 24, max: 72)\",\n",
    "                    \"default\": 24\n",
    "                }\n",
    "            },\n",
    "            \"required\": [\"account_id\"]\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    }\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Sandbox: {len(TOOL_DEFINITIONS)} tools registered\")\n",
    "for t in TOOL_DEFINITIONS:\n",
    "    print(f\"  - {t['name']}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Mock Tool Implementations (DEMO_MODE)\n",
    "\n",
    "In DEMO_MODE, each tool returns realistic mock data. In production, replace these with real implementations that carry isolated credentials."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def _mock_lookup_account(account_id: str) -> dict:\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"account_id\": account_id,\n",
    "        \"status\": \"in_use\",\n",
    "        \"lab_type\": \"AWS_EC2_Advanced\",\n",
    "        \"assigned_at\": \"2026-05-16T06:00:00Z\",\n",
    "        \"expires_at\": \"2026-05-16T10:00:00Z\",\n",
    "        \"history\": [\n",
    "            {\"lab_type\": \"AWS_EC2_Advanced\", \"duration_seconds\": 14400, \"assigned_at\": \"2026-05-16T06:00:00Z\"},\n",
    "            {\"lab_type\": \"AWS_S3_Basic\", \"duration_seconds\": 7200, \"assigned_at\": \"2026-05-15T10:00:00Z\"}\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _mock_lookup_policy(account_id: str, action: str | None = None) -> dict:\n",
    "    deny_rules = [\n",
    "        {\n",
    "            \"policy\": \"sandbox-restrictions\",\n",
    "            \"actions\": [\"ec2:RunInstances\", \"ec2:CreateNatGateway\", \"ec2:CreateTransitGateway\"],\n",
    "            \"condition\": None\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    if action:\n",
    "        deny_rules = [r for r in deny_rules if any(a == action or a == \"*\" for a in r[\"actions\"])]\n",
    "\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"account_id\": account_id,\n",
    "        \"policy_count\": 3,\n",
    "        \"deny_rules\": deny_rules,\n",
    "        \"deny_summary\": \"sandbox-restrictions denies: ec2:RunInstances, ec2:CreateNatGateway, ec2:CreateTransitGateway\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _mock_get_audit_trail(account_id: str, hours: int = 24) -> dict:\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"account_id\": account_id,\n",
    "        \"hours\": hours,\n",
    "        \"event_count\": 3,\n",
    "        \"events\": [\n",
    "            {\"time\": \"2026-05-16T08:30:00Z\", \"action\": \"ec2:RunInstances\", \"user\": \"lab-user\", \"source_ip\": \"203.0.113.42\", \"resource\": None},\n",
    "            {\"time\": \"2026-05-16T08:29:00Z\", \"action\": \"ec2:DescribeInstances\", \"user\": \"lab-user\", \"source_ip\": \"203.0.113.42\", \"resource\": None},\n",
    "            {\"time\": \"2026-05-16T07:00:00Z\", \"action\": \"sts:AssumeRole\", \"user\": \"lab-user\", \"source_ip\": \"203.0.113.42\", \"resource\": \"arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/lab-role\"}\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Mock tools ready\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Sandbox Dispatcher\n",
    "\n",
    "The dispatcher is the core of the sandbox boundary. It validates every tool call against the allowlist before execution — Claude cannot call anything not in `_REGISTRY`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Sandbox registry — only tools listed here are callable ────────────────────\n",
    "_REGISTRY: dict[str, Any] = {\n",
    "    \"lookup_account\":   _mock_lookup_account   if DEMO_MODE else None,  # replace with real impl\n",
    "    \"lookup_policy\":    _mock_lookup_policy    if DEMO_MODE else None,\n",
    "    \"get_audit_trail\":  _mock_get_audit_trail  if DEMO_MODE else None,\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def dispatch(tool_name: str, tool_input: dict) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Execute a sandboxed tool call.\n",
    "    Raises ValueError if tool_name is not in the registry — Claude cannot escape the sandbox.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    if tool_name not in _REGISTRY:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"Tool '{tool_name}' is not registered in the sandbox\")\n",
    "    fn = _REGISTRY[tool_name]\n",
    "    if fn is None:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError(f\"Tool '{tool_name}' has no implementation — set DEMO_MODE=True or wire a real impl\")\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        result = fn(**tool_input)\n",
    "        return json.dumps(result, default=str)\n",
    "    except Exception as exc:\n",
    "        return json.dumps({\"error\": str(exc)})\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Dispatcher ready — {len(_REGISTRY)} tools in sandbox\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## System Prompt\n",
    "\n",
    "The system prompt tells Claude what it is, what tools it has, and what it cannot do. Read-only constraint is explicit — Claude should never suggest write operations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SYSTEM_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are an infrastructure support intelligence agent.\n",
    "\n",
    "You have access to exactly three live tools:\n",
    "- lookup_account   — current account state and assignment history\n",
    "- lookup_policy    — active policy evaluation (what is denied and why)\n",
    "- get_audit_trail  — recent activity inside an account\n",
    "\n",
    "Rules:\n",
    "- Always look up live data before answering — never guess account state\n",
    "- If a tool returns an error, say so clearly and suggest next steps\n",
    "- Be concise — support engineers read your output in real time\n",
    "- You are read-only — never suggest actions that require write access\n",
    "- If the issue is beyond what your tools can diagnose, say so explicitly\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"System prompt configured\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Agent Loop\n",
    "\n",
    "The agentic loop runs Claude, dispatches tool calls through the sandbox, feeds results back, and continues until Claude produces a final answer with no tool calls."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def run_sandboxed_agent(query: str, verbose: bool = True) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Run Claude inside the sandbox and return the final response.\n",
    "    All tool calls are validated by the dispatcher before execution.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    messages = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": query}]\n",
    "    turn = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "    while True:\n",
    "        turn += 1\n",
    "        if verbose:\n",
    "            print(f\"\\n── Turn {turn} ────────────────────────────\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        response = client.messages.create(\n",
    "            model=MODEL,\n",
    "            max_tokens=2048,\n",
    "            system=SYSTEM_PROMPT,\n",
    "            tools=TOOL_DEFINITIONS,\n",
    "            messages=messages,\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Collect text output\n",
    "        for block in response.content:\n",
    "            if hasattr(block, \"text\") and verbose:\n",
    "                print(f\"Claude: {block.text}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        # No tool calls → final answer\n",
    "        if response.stop_reason != \"tool_use\":\n",
    "            final = \" \".join(\n",
    "                block.text for block in response.content if hasattr(block, \"text\")\n",
    "            )\n",
    "            return final\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Dispatch tool calls through sandbox\n",
    "        tool_results = []\n",
    "        for block in response.content:\n",
    "            if block.type != \"tool_use\":\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            if verbose:\n",
    "                print(f\"  → tool call: {block.name}({json.dumps(block.input)})\")\n",
    "            result = dispatch(block.name, block.input)\n",
    "            if verbose:\n",
    "                parsed = json.loads(result)\n",
    "                print(f\"  ← result: {json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)[:400]}\")\n",
    "            tool_results.append({\n",
    "                \"type\": \"tool_result\",\n",
    "                \"tool_use_id\": block.id,\n",
    "                \"content\": result,\n",
    "            })\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Feed results back for next turn\n",
    "        messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n",
    "        messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": tool_results})\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Agent ready\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Example 1 — Policy Denial Diagnosis\n",
    "\n",
    "A support engineer asks why an account can't run EC2 instances. Claude calls `lookup_account` to confirm the account exists, then `lookup_policy` with the specific action to identify the deny rule."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "query = \"Why can't account 123456789012 run EC2 instances? The learner says they get an access denied error.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "answer = run_sandboxed_agent(query, verbose=True)\n",
    "print(f\"\\n── Final Answer ────────────────────────\")\n",
    "print(answer)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Example 2 — Recent Activity Audit\n",
    "\n",
    "A support engineer suspects unusual activity. Claude calls `lookup_account` to confirm status, then `get_audit_trail` to surface recent events."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "query = \"Account 123456789012 — what has the user been doing in the last 2 hours? Any failed actions?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "answer = run_sandboxed_agent(query, verbose=True)\n",
    "print(f\"\\n── Final Answer ────────────────────────\")\n",
    "print(answer)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Example 3 — Sandbox Boundary Test\n",
    "\n",
    "Verify the sandbox rejects calls to unregistered tools. Claude only has three tools — any attempt to call outside that boundary raises an error."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Directly test the sandbox boundary — this should raise ValueError\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    dispatch(\"delete_account\", {\"account_id\": \"123456789012\"})\n",
    "    print(\"ERROR: sandbox did not block the call\")\n",
    "except ValueError as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Sandbox blocked: {e}\")\n",
    "    print(\"Boundary enforcement working correctly\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Key Design Decisions\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why allowlist, not blocklist?\n",
    "Blocklists require you to enumerate every dangerous operation upfront. Allowlists are safer by default — if a tool isn't registered, Claude can't call it, regardless of what it tries.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why per-tool credential isolation?\n",
    "If `lookup_policy`'s read-only AWS credentials are leaked, the attacker cannot use them to read MongoDB or assume arbitrary roles. Each tool has the minimum credential scope needed for its job.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why three tools and not more?\n",
    "Blast radius control. Each tool added to the sandbox is a new attack surface. Three tools covering account state, policy, and audit trail answer 95% of support questions.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why no write tools at all?\n",
    "Read-only answers most support questions. When write access is genuinely needed, it should go through a separate, audited path — not through the support agent's sandbox.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Production wiring\n",
    "\n",
    "To move from DEMO_MODE to production:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Implement `lookup_account` with a read-only MongoDB connection string\n",
    "2. Implement `lookup_policy` with a read-only AWS org profile\n",
    "3. Implement `get_audit_trail` with STS assume-role scoped per account\n",
    "4. Replace `_mock_*` functions in `_REGISTRY` with the real implementations\n",
    "5. Set `DEMO_MODE = False`\n",
    "\n",
    "See [claude-sandboxed-agent](https://github.com/TanishkaMarrott/claude-sandboxed-agent) for a full production implementation with WebSocket streaming and Firebase auth."
   ]
  }
 ]
}"
